---
title: 'Large Dataset Interactivity'
---

AG Charts allows displaying and exploring large datasets using all features and options, and without having to add any special configurations.

Using aggregation strategies such as [the M4 algorithm](https://blog.ag-grid.com/optimizing-large-data-set-visualisations-with-the-m4-algorithm/),
an accurate representation of large data is shown for all series and axes types.

This approach adapts seamlessly to different levels of granularity, allowing users to explore the data with all of the functionality
available in AG Charts, including [Zoom](./zoom/), [Navigator](./navigator/) and [Tooltips](./tooltip).

{% chartExampleRunner title="Ordered Data" name="ordered-data" type="generated" /%}

In the above example:

-   Use the controls to select different series types and data sizes.
-   Use the mouse or controls to zoom and pan the data.
-   This is a basic example - other axis and series types and options are also available.
